Z||000000||Vlad||08-27-2001||01:49 AM||||Hello guys,<P>What would make the steering wheel to move by itseft on the bampy roads?<P>It's fine on the good pavment at any speeds, but onse I go over the bumps I really have to hold the steering wheel hard with both hands.<P>I have a play in the right lower ball joint, buy the question is if it is the only problem that makes the steering wheel turn.<P>Thanks<P>85 GT<P>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Vlad||08-27-2001||01:50 AM||||Ops.......<P>What a funny subject line.....:-)<P>Sorry about that.||||reg||1
Z||000002||maryjane||08-27-2001||02:47 AM||||A bad steeering damper will contribute to your feeling the rough road in the wheel, but I would be WAY more concerned about the bad ball joint. If it goes,  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_watchout.gif"> lookout ditch, here we come!||||reg||1
Z||000003||mrfiero||08-27-2001||02:59 AM||||Bad lower balljoints will make the car wander a lot.  If they're really loose then any and all irregularities in the road will cause problems (white knuckle driving!).<P>I would replace the lower balljoints (always replace them in pairs) and inspect/replace the steering damper/shock thing too.  ||||reg||1
